<FictionBook xmlns="http://www.gribuser.ru/xml/fictionbook/2.0" xmlns:l="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><description><title-info><genre>unrecognised</genre><author><first-name>Mara</first-name><last-name>Quill</last-name></author><book-title>The Lighthouse Keeper</book-title><date>2026-05-01</date><coverpage><image l:href="#image1" l:type="inlineImageType" alt="" /></coverpage><lang>en</lang></title-info><document-info><program-used>pandoc</program-used></document-info></description><body><title><p>The Lighthouse Keeper</p></title><section id="arrival"><title><p>Arrival</p></title><p>The boat left her on the rocks at dawn, with a trunk and a lamp.</p><p>She climbed the <emphasis>ninety-nine</emphasis> steps and found the <strong>logbook</strong> open.</p></section><section id="storm"><title><p>Storm</p></title><p>Wind came over the cape before noon. The glass fell all afternoon.</p><image l:href="#image2" l:type="imageType" alt="The beam" /><section id="the-lamp"><title><p>The Lamp</p></title><p>She trimmed the wick twice before midnight.</p></section></section><section id="morning"><title><p>Morning</p></title><p>Gulls, salt, and a calm grey sea.</p></section></body><binary id="image2" content-type="image/png"></binary><binary id="image1" content-type="image/jpeg"></binary></FictionBook>
